- **B1105-3 (Major).** The isolation scan (`TemplateIsolationTests.cs:14`) is a deny-list on `QuoteStore`, `Quote*Dto` and others; a planted `QuoteFileStore.SaveQuote(null!)` passed with all 291 rows green. Fix: an **allow-list**. Property: the Templates code may name a type starting `Quote`, `Snapshot`, `Version`, `Persisted`, `Purchase`, `Fleet` or `Calculation` only through the exact static helpers it needs today. **At least:** `QuoteFileStore.(ResolvePrivate|ResolveHosted|CreatePrivateDirectory|Write)`, `QuotePersistence.HostedRootKey`, `QuoteEndpoints.(Authorized|Read)`; list the names the code uses today BY PROGRAM at the pin and allow exactly those; any other `Quote*` name is a finding of the scan. **Any other shape of allow-list: prove it meets the property or STOP.** Correct the test's summary (`:5-10`) so it says what is scanned. Test: the control must plant `f.SaveQuote(null!)` on a `QuoteFileStore` and fail, and a planted `QuotePersistence` call to a non-allowed member must fail (both inside the existing control test, `:42-54`).
- **B1105-4 (Major).** (a) `NameOk` (`TemplateRules.cs:16-17`) accepts U+2028/U+2029 (categories Zl, Zp, not Cc): refuse them, keep everything else. The 400 sentence at `TemplateEndpoints.cs:229` already says "no line breaks": do not change it. Test: `{"name":"a b"}` and the U+2029 form 400 on POST and PUT, and a stored-file case is refused at start by `WellFormed` (it calls `NameOk`; prove it). (b) `docs/API.md:844` "no line break" stays true now; `:847`: reword to "a `baseVersion` of 1 or more that is not the latest is 409 `STALE_REVISION`; below 1 is 400"; and the contract text that repeats "any other value is 409" (`openapi.json`, the PUT description near `:519`): same wording ("of 1 or more"). Both sentences use the words "of 1 or more".
- **B1105-5 (Minor).** `GET .../{id}`, `GET .../versions/{n}`, `POST .../archive` answer 400 `ACT_AS_INVALID` and do not document 400 (the only 3 of 43 operations without it). Fix: three contract response rows (`openapi.json:501`, `:534`, `:549`), copying the wording the other operations use (reuse an existing description; list it as reused), then re-sync in commit B. `Contract.Check` must stay green; add a row that sends an invalid act-as header to each of the three and is checked by `Contract` (also pin `Acting_as_a_role...` at `TemplateApiTests.cs:370`, which accepts 400 or 403, to the status the build answers).
